# Store text as LF in the repository and check it out as LF on every platform, so that a Windows
# checkout is byte-identical to a Linux one regardless of core.autocrlf. Binary files are detected
# automatically. (A file that a Windows program later rewrites with CRLF can still show as modified
# until it is re-added; the generated manifest is therefore written with LF explicitly.)
#
# Every tracked text file is stored with LF. (Four CSV files with CRLF row terminators once
# lived here and are gone; if a file with CRLF is ever committed again, git leaves it alone
# under text=auto, and "git add --renormalize ." would rewrite it - check "git diff --cached
# --stat" first.)
* text=auto eol=lf
